        "matched_product": "cast iron skillet",
        "snippet": "The Best Small Cast Iron Skillet: Field Company No.5 Cast Iron Chef Skillet at Fieldcompany.com Jump to Review · I tested cast iron skillets by searing and baking in them, noting if anything stuck egregiously to the surface. Cast iron skillets are dead simple pieces of cookware. They’re cast out of an alloy of iron, carbon, and silicon that is sanded and sometimes pre-seasoned. Sure, like most gear, the design and price tag vary depending on the manufacturer, but at their core, cast iron skillets are just a big honkin’ piece of metal. The Best Small Cast Iron Skillet: Field Company No.5 Cast Iron Chef Skillet at Fieldcompany.com Jump to Review · I tested cast iron skillets by searing and baking in them, noting if anything stuck egregiously to the surface. The best cast iron skillet is from Lodge. It heats up fast and sears deeply, and only costs around $20. We also like the lightweight Lancaster No. Options abound: pricey and cheap, smooth-surfaced or pebbled, big and small. But much of what makes a great cast iron skillet boils down to a cook’s preferences.",
